Number = {5},
Pages = {703-716},
Abstract = {Warren Mitofsky and Joseph Waksberg were two of the most influential
   researchers in telephone surveys and survey research methods. Their
   development of the Mitofsky-Waksberg method for random digit dialing
   sampling revolutionized telephone sampling and surveys. Jointly and
   separately, Waksberg and Mitofsky were instrumental in the development
   of many innovative methods and applications. This article reviews some
   of their contributions and discusses how their approaches to these
   problems may be a model for addressing issues that are being encountered
   currently in the United States in cell phone research.},
